9fc94ae574ef6c937bdbd119a3156438bd7-1024x1024.png%3Fw%3D128%26h%3D128%26fit%3Dcrop%26auto%3Dformat&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div></div></div><div class="pointer-events-none relative z-10 flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 overflow-hidden"><p class="typ-caption-1 text-grey-400 mt-6 line-clamp-1" title="Nitesh Shah, Aneeka Gupta">Nitesh Shah, Aneeka Gupta</p><h4 class="typ-h4 text-navy-300 line-clamp-3 first:mt-4" title="What&#x27;s Hot: Wheat&#x27;s war premium returns">What&#x27;s Hot: Wheat&#x27;s war premium returns</h4><time dateTime="2026-09-04" class="typ-caption-2 text-grey-300">4 September 2026</time><p class="typ-body text-navy-300 line-clamp-3">Wheat has rallied sharply as Black Sea disruptions tighten export capacity during the peak shipping window, while speculative investors remain net short. With El Niño threatening Southern Hemisphere supply and the forward curve still in contango, the market is pricing a war premium without fully positioning for a sustained shortage. </p><ul class="mt-4 list-none p-0 flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-label="Tags"><li class="typ-caption-2 border-grey-100 text-navy-300 inline-flex max-w-full items-center border px-2 py-1"><span class="truncate">Agricultural Commodities</span></li><li class="typ-caption-2 border-grey-100 text-navy-300 inline-flex max-w-full items-center border px-2 py-1"><span class="truncate">Commodities</span></li></ul></div></div></a></div></li><li class="splide__slide pb-1"><div class="h-full"><a aria-label="Commodity Outlook: The baton never drops but who carries it keeps changing" class="group relative block h-full focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-grey-100 focus-visible:ring-offset-2" href="/gb/insights/blog/commodity-outlook-the-baton-never-drops-but-who-carries-it-keeps-changing"><div class="border-grey-100 group-hover:border-grey-200 flex h-full flex-col border bg-white p-3 transition-colors duration-200 md:p-4"><div class="pointer-events-none relative h-52 w-full"><div class="re